-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- D over codes (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.13 “F31–F32 — Reflection and certificates”, its part F31: D : Code → Code)
-- a code of the fragment — the variable 0 under one λ, plus, times, Nat literals — read as a
-- polynomial through lib/ring.cub's bridge (an expression in the variable 0), differentiated by
-- D, and written as a code again: the derivative of a program is a program, and taylor is the
-- theorem about what it denotes. The bridge is unverified (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.13 “F31–F32 — Reflection and certificates”); D and taylor are checked
pl-of-ex : Ex → Opt Pl
pl-of-ex (ec n) = some (kc n)
pl-of-ex (ev v) = if weq v #0 then some kx else none
pl-of-ex (eadd a b) = (case pl-of-ex a of none → none; some pa → (case pl-of-ex b of none → none; some pb → some (kadd pa pb)))
pl-of-ex (emul a b) = (case pl-of-ex a of none → none; some pa → (case pl-of-ex b of none → none; some pb → some (kmul pa pb)))
